  "headline": "Indonesia Formally Enacts Asset Seizure Law For Criminal Offenses",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Enacts Asset Seizure Law",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has passed a law on asset seizure for criminal cases, aiming to aid state recovery and compensate victims.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The new law allows for the seizure of assets linked to corruption and other criminal acts to compensate victims and restore state finances.",
    "Two specialized agencies will be established to manage the seized assets, though the law will only apply to future cases rather than past offenses.",
    "Government officials and the Corruption Eradication Commission have expressed support for the measure as a tool for anti-corruption efforts."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has officially passed the Law on Asset Seizure for Criminal Cases, a legislative move designed to address corruption and other illegal activities. According to reports, the legislation includes mechanisms to recover state losses and provide compensation to victims of fraud, such as investment scams and travel industry disputes. While the law is intended to strengthen enforcement, officials noted that it does not apply retroactively to past crimes. Full implementation is expected to follow a 12-month waiting period, during which two specialized government agencies will be established to oversee the management of confiscated property. Members of the legislative leadership and the Corruption Eradication Commission have praised the act as a significant development in the country's anti-corruption strategy, though discussions remain regarding specific legal provisions like illicit enrichment.",
